    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet on an elevated site along the renowned Wicklow Way, Raheengraney enjoys sweeping countryside views across the Wicklow, Wexford and Carlow borders.\n\nBuilt circa 1983 and extending to approximately 113.7 sq. m., this substantial four-bedroom detached bungalow offers spacious and versatile accommodation comprising a kitchen/dining room, a large living room, four bedrooms and a family bathroom.\n\nThe residence benefits from oil-fired central heating, together with a back boiler in the living room. Private services include an on-site well and septic tank.\n\nSet on a site extending to approximately C.0.916 acres, the property is approached through a walled entrance onto a tarmacadam driveway. A concrete yard lies to the rear, while the grounds also include a double garage, numerous useful outbuildings and a dedicated orchard area.\n\nOffering generous accommodation, extensive outbuildings and considerable potential in a wonderfully scenic setting, Raheengraney presents an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a countryside home within easy reach of Clonegal and the surrounding counties.\n\nThe property may also qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, subject to the purchaser satisfying the relevant eligibility criteria."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - 3.71m x 8.33m\nA welcoming entrance hallway featuring tiled flooring and neutral décor.\n\nLiving Room: - 4.34m x 5.48m\nA bright and spacious reception room featuring timber-effect laminate flooring, a marble fireplace with an open fire and back boiler, and a large window overlooking the front of the property. Solid-wood built-in alcove units provide ample storage and integrated bookshelves.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room: - 6.59m x 3.01m\nA bright and spacious triple-aspect room allowing natural light to flood the space. The kitchen area features tiled flooring, solid-wood fitted units, laminate worktops, a tiled splashback, gas hob and electric oven. The adjoining dining area is finished with carpeted flooring and offers ample space for family dining.\n\nBedroom 4: - 2.94m x 3.54m\nBedroom with a window overlooking the rear of the property.\n\nBathroom: - 2.78m x 1.83m\nTiled flooring, panelled walls, blue sanitary ware and an electric shower.\n\nBedroom 3: - 2.78m x 2.72m\nTimber-effect tiled flooring and a window overlooking the rear of the property.\n\nBedroom 2: - 3.77m x 3.02m\nWindow overlooking the rear of the property and built-in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.94-m x 4.08m\nLarge and spacious bedroom positioned to the front of the property, with carpeted flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\n"
      },
